WEBVTT

00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:03.900
Actae. A refund that survives a crash.

00:00:04.000 --> 00:00:08.900
The agent reads the order, records its decision, and calls the payment provider.

00:00:09.500 --> 00:00:16.700
At eight seconds the worker is killed. The refund has landed. The result was never recorded.

00:00:19.000 --> 00:00:23.900
On restart, the ledger reclaims the operation with a fencing token.

00:00:24.000 --> 00:00:31.800
The retry presents the same idempotency key, so the provider returns the recorded refund instead of charging again.

00:00:33.000 --> 00:00:38.400
In the dashboard, this run now shows two attempts of the same payment operation.

00:00:40.000 --> 00:00:46.100
Attempt two is the reclaim. The inspector shows the key and the original refund.

00:00:59.000 --> 00:01:05.000
Now a fork. Keep the prefix, and change the decision at the boundary.

00:01:06.000 --> 00:01:13.600
The child run applies a partial refund. The confirmation email is inherited and replayed, never resent.

00:01:22.000 --> 00:01:29.100
The fork event records the boundary, the reason, and the inherited state. The original run is untouched.

00:01:30.000 --> 00:01:35.300
One charge, one email, and a second branch you can compare, then promote.
